Radeon RX 550 on a big-endian Power Mac G5 - Arch POWER (ppc64)
================================================================

Packages
--------
  linux-ppc64-rx550g5
      Linux 7.2.12 with Arch POWER's linux-ppc64 configuration (64 KiB pages, ELFv2) and the
      big-endian amdgpu patches (command, MQD and ring byte order, display, VBIOS tables, HDMI/DP
      info packets, VCE ring wrap, soft recovery) plus g5_cpu_temp. It installs next to
      linux-ppc64, which stays in the GRUB "Advanced options" menu as a fallback.
  mesa-rx550g5 vulkan-radeon-rx550g5 vulkan-swrast-rx550g5 vulkan-mesa-layers-rx550g5
  opencl-mesa-rx550g5
      Mesa 26.2.6 with the big-endian GFX8 fixes (radeonsi on LLVM, RADV, Rusticl). Each one
      provides and conflicts with the Arch package of the same base name (mesa, vulkan-radeon, ...),
      so pacman asks to replace the stock package on install, and an Arch Mesa update does not
      replace it later.
  rx550-g5 (this package)
      Boot integration, driver options and X configuration.

Install
-------
  sudo pacman -S --needed linux-firmware-amdgpu
  sudo pacman -U ./*.pkg.tar.zst        (all files from the release; answer y to replace mesa etc.)
  sudo reboot

Keep the original graphics card (GeForce 6600 or similar) installed and connected: the G5
firmware needs it to boot. The RX 550 drives the desktop.

What this package does
----------------------
* Makes GRUB start linux-ppc64-rx550g5 by default: /etc/default/grub.d/90-rx550-g5.cfg sets
  GRUB_TOP_LEVEL, and a pacman hook runs grub-mkconfig after the kernel is installed or updated.
  Removing the package restores the previous order.
* rx550-g5.service loads amdgpu after boot and before the display manager. amdgpu is
  blacklisted for automatic loading so that a GPU problem never stops the machine from booting:
  if a probe is interrupted (hang, crash, power loss), /var/lib/rx550-g5/probe-in-progress stops
  further automatic attempts. Delete it to try again.
* Driver options (/usr/lib/modprobe.d/rx550-g5.conf):
    runpm=0            keep the GPU powered (hotplug while suspended untested)
    gpu_recovery=0     full GPU reset fails on the G5; soft recovery still runs
    lockup_timeout=10000  valid long jobs take more than the 2 s default
    ttm pages_limit=24576  GPU system memory goes through the 2 GB DART window that SATA,
                       network, USB and audio share; cap at 1.5 GB (64 KiB pages)
* X: the modesetting driver with a software cursor for amdgpu devices
  (/usr/share/X11/xorg.conf.d/20-rx550-g5.conf). Files in /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d take precedence.
* An output connected after X started is switched on if nothing else is lit.

Recovery
--------
* Append rx550.disable=1 to the kernel command line in GRUB (press e) to skip loading amdgpu,
  or pick linux-ppc64 under "Advanced options".
* To return to stock: sudo pacman -S mesa vulkan-radeon opencl-mesa (answer y to replace), then
  sudo pacman -R rx550-g5 linux-ppc64-rx550g5.

Video and OpenCL
----------------
VA-API decode (H.264, HEVC 8/10-bit, MPEG-2) and VCE encode (H.264, HEVC). Mesa 26 has no VDPAU.
OpenCL: opencl-mesa-rx550g5 (Rusticl on radeonsi); fp64 needs RUSTICL_FEATURES=fp64.
